From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Arun Iyengar <aiyengar1990@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 1 Nov 2026 22:30:00 +0000
Subject: wireless: uwe5622: do not report a missing bt_hostwake DT node as an error

The Allwinner build of the WCN core (CONFIG_AW_BOARD + CONFIG_BT_WAKE_HOST_EN,
unisocwcn/Makefile) registers the BT_WAKE_AP pin as a wake-up IRQ from a DT
node with compatible "allwinner,sunxi-btlpm" (vendor BSP style). Mainline
device trees of the Orange Pi Zero2/Zero2W/Zero3 and WalnutPi boards do not
have that node, so every boot logs

  WCN_ERR: dts node for bt_wake not found

although nothing is wrong: marlin_probe() continues ("marlin2 parse_dt some
para not config"), WiFi and Bluetooth work, only the host cannot be woken by
Bluetooth from suspend.

Log it once at info level and return -ENODEV, and guard the suspend/resume
hooks so they do not call enable_irq()/disable_irq() on IRQ 0 when no pin was
registered. Behaviour is otherwise unchanged (the BT_WAKE_HOST bit sent to the
firmware stays as before).

To actually use the pin on the Orange Pi Zero2 (vendor DT: bt_hostwake PG16,
bt_wake PG17, bt_rst_n PG19, wlan_hostwake PG15) a node like

  bt-lpm { compatible = "allwinner,sunxi-btlpm";
           bt_hostwake-gpios = <&pio 6 16 GPIO_ACTIVE_HIGH>; };

would be needed; the >= 7.1 code path looks the GPIO up with
fwnode_gpiod_get_index(..., "bt_hostwake", ...), i.e. a -gpios suffix.

Upstream: to be submitted to https://github.com/armbian/uwe5622
Assisted-by: LLM
Signed-off-by: Arun Iyengar <aiyengar1990@gmail.com>
---
 drivers/net/wireless/uwe5622/unisocwcn/platform/wcn_boot.c | 26 ++++++++++++++++++++------
 1 file changed, 20 insertions(+), 6 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/net/wireless/uwe5622/unisocwcn/platform/wcn_boot.c b/drivers/net/wireless/uwe5622/unisocwcn/platform/wcn_boot.c
index c6eeb84..5cdb5c3 100644
--- a/drivers/net/wireless/uwe5622/unisocwcn/platform/wcn_boot.c
+++ b/drivers/net/wireless/uwe5622/unisocwcn/platform/wcn_boot.c
@@ -1432,12 +1432,14 @@ OUT:
 #ifdef CONFIG_AW_BOARD
 static void marlin_bt_wake_int_en(void)
 {
-	enable_irq(marlin_dev->bt_wake_host_int_num);
+	if (marlin_dev->bt_wake_host_int_num)
+		enable_irq(marlin_dev->bt_wake_host_int_num);
 }
 
 static void marlin_bt_wake_int_dis(void)
 {
-	disable_irq(marlin_dev->bt_wake_host_int_num);
+	if (marlin_dev->bt_wake_host_int_num)
+		disable_irq(marlin_dev->bt_wake_host_int_num);
 }
 
 static irqreturn_t marlin_bt_wake_int_isr(int irq, void *para)
@@ -1458,8 +1460,14 @@ static int __maybe_unused marlin_registsr_bt_wake(struct device *dev)
 
 	np = of_find_compatible_node(NULL, NULL, "allwinner,sunxi-btlpm");
 	if (!np) {
-		WCN_ERR("dts node for bt_wake not found");
-		return -EINVAL;
+		/*
+		 * Optional: mainline device trees (Orange Pi Zero2/Zero3,
+		 * WalnutPi, ...) do not describe the BT_WAKE_AP pin. The chip
+		 * works without it, only Bluetooth cannot wake the host from
+		 * suspend. Not an error.
+		 */
+		WCN_INFO("no allwinner,sunxi-btlpm node, bt_hostwake irq not used\n");
+		return -ENODEV;
 	}
 	bt_wake_host_gpio = fwnode_gpiod_get_index(of_fwnode_handle(np),
 				"bt_hostwake", 0, GPIOD_IN, "bt-wake-host-gpio");
@@ -1506,8 +1514,14 @@ static int __maybe_unused marlin_registsr_bt_wake(struct device *dev)
 
 	np = of_find_compatible_node(NULL, NULL, "allwinner,sunxi-btlpm");
 	if (!np) {
-		WCN_ERR("dts node for bt_wake not found");
-		return -EINVAL;
+		/*
+		 * Optional: mainline device trees (Orange Pi Zero2/Zero3,
+		 * WalnutPi, ...) do not describe the BT_WAKE_AP pin. The chip
+		 * works without it, only Bluetooth cannot wake the host from
+		 * suspend. Not an error.
+		 */
+		WCN_INFO("no allwinner,sunxi-btlpm node, bt_hostwake irq not used\n");
+		return -ENODEV;
 	}
 	bt_wake_host_gpio = of_get_named_gpio(np, "bt_hostwake", 0);
 	if (!gpio_is_valid(bt_wake_host_gpio)) {
